(The French Revolution \(1789-1799\) - Revision Sheet) Tj T*
(History 201. Causes, timeline, key figures, vocabulary.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Long-term Causes) Tj T*
(Financial crisis: decades of war debt \(including support for the) Tj T*
(American Revolution\) plus an unfair tax system.) Tj T*
(Social structure: the Three Estates - clergy \(1st\), nobility \(2nd\),) Tj T*
(everyone else \(3rd, about 97% of the population, paying most taxes\).) Tj T*
(Enlightenment ideas: Rousseau, Voltaire and Montesquieu questioned) Tj T*
(absolute monarchy and promoted popular sovereignty.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Timeline) Tj T*
(May 1789: Estates-General convenes at Versailles for the first time) Tj T*
(since 1614. June 1789: Third Estate declares itself the National) Tj T*
(Assembly \(Tennis Court Oath\).) Tj T*
(July 14, 1789: Storming of the Bastille - the symbolic start.) Tj T*
(August 1789: Declaration of the Rights of Man and of the Citizen.) Tj T*
(1791: First constitution; Louis XVI's failed Flight to Varennes.) Tj T*
(1792: Monarchy abolished; First Republic proclaimed.) Tj T*
(January 1793: Execution of Louis XVI by guillotine.) Tj T*
(1793-1794: Reign of Terror under Robespierre and the Committee of) Tj T*
(Public Safety - about 17,000 official executions.) Tj T*
(July 1794: Thermidorian Reaction - Robespierre falls and is executed.) Tj T*
(1795-1799: The Directory, a five-man executive, rules unstable France.) Tj T*
(November 1799: Napoleon's coup of 18 Brumaire ends the Revolution.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Key Figures) Tj T*
(Louis XVI: king executed in 1793. Marie Antoinette: queen, executed) Tj T*
(the same year. Robespierre: architect of the Terror. Danton: early) Tj T*
(revolutionary leader, later guillotined. Napoleon Bonaparte: general) Tj T*
(who seized power in 1799.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Vocabulary) Tj T*
(Bastille: royal fortress-prison in Paris. Guillotine: execution) Tj T*
(device adopted as a 'humane' method. Sans-culottes: radical working) Tj T*
(class militants. Emigres: nobles who fled abroad. Jacobins: the) Tj T*
(radical political club that dominated the Terror.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
